 <p>The Patriots jumped out to a 6-0 lead in the opening set but couldn&#8217;t hold it, falling behind 0-2 in the match. From there, Lewisburg dug in — battling from behind to take a tight fourth set 26-24 and force a decisive fifth, which the Patriots dominated 15-7 to seal the North Half crown.</p>
 <p>Addison Cole powered the comeback with a monster all-around night: 32 kills, 16 assists and 17 digs. Hadleigh Woods anchored the defense with 33 digs to go with 6 assists and 3 aces, while Presley Meadows ran the offense with 32 assists, 13 digs and 2 aces.</p>
 <p>The win moves Lewisburg to 34-8 on the season — and avenges a 3-2 loss to Germantown back on August 20.</p>
